{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>If a man takes a wife and comes to her and hates her</b> — the reason is: when a man takes a woman by the acquisitions of the Torah, which are kiddushin by money, and she is the betrothed (me'orasah) whom he mentions (Deuteronomy 22:23), and after some time he comes to her and hates her, because she was not pleasing to him in her conjugal relations, and he rises early in the morning and comes to court and claims that he did not find her a virgin. Now this one intends to divorce her without the mohar of virgins, which is the ketubah that he wrote for her, and because she entered his kiddushin with the presumption of virginity, he claims against her that she committed adultery under him. Therefore Scripture says (Deuteronomy 22:20), <b>but if the matter was true</b> — according to the husband's words — <b>they shall stone her</b>. And the truth shall not be known except by the testimony of two witnesses. And since Scripture specifies in the case of the betrothed virgin's fornication that when she is betrothed she is stoned and when she is not betrothed she is exempt, it was unnecessary to specify here: 'but if the matter was true, that she committed adultery during her betrothal and that she committed adultery of her own will — they shall stone her.' Instead, he said it by allusion (Deuteronomy 22:21): because she has done a vile thing (nevalah) in Israel, by playing the harlot in her father's house. And the 'vile thing' (nevalah) is in her doing so of her own will." "And <b>to play the harlot</b> (liznot) — this is when a married woman commits adultery under her husband, for a young woman who is not betrothed is not called a <b>zonah</b> when she lies with one of the people; rather, she is designated for him (Exodus 22:15)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Deuteronomy 22:21, not 22:11 as appears in the source text; this is clearly a typographical error in the Hebrew, and I have corrected the verse reference accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:00.686955426Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}